{"tool_name":"iguide","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"iGUIDE","home":"https://github.com/cnobles/iGUIDE","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Improved pipeline for analyzing CRISPR cleavage specificity.","addition_date":"2019-05-25T15:48:54Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:22Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:iGUIDE","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"chris.l.nobles@gmail.com","name":"Chris Nobles","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://iguide.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"PCR primer design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0308"},{"term":"Scaffolding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3216"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"iGUIDE","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-019-1625-3","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 The Author(s).Genome engineering methods have advanced greatly with the development of programmable nucleases, but methods for quantifying on- and off-target cleavage sites and associated deletions remain nascent. Here, we report an improvement of the GUIDE-seq method, iGUIDE, which allows filtering of mispriming events to clarify the true cleavage signal. Using iGUIDE, we specify the locations of Cas9-guided cleavage for four guide RNAs, characterize associated deletions, and show that naturally occurring background DNA double-strand breaks are associated with open chromatin, gene dense regions, and chromosomal fragile sites. iGUIDE is available from https://github.com/cnobles/iGUIDE.","authors":[{"name":"Bushman F.D."},{"name":"Davis M.M."},{"name":"June C.H."},{"name":"Liu X."},{"name":"Melenhorst J.J."},{"name":"Nobles C.L."},{"name":"Reddy